    "description": "Accountability isn't a built-in language feature: it's a development practice. It means writing code in a way that makes it clear who did what, what happened, and why, so actions can be traced and owned.\n\nAccountability may take several shapes: \n\n+ Logging actions\n+ Audit trails\n+ Reporting errors\n+ Adding tests\n+ Using VCS\n+ Code reviews.\n",
